SUMMARY:Lunch and Learn: Build Skills — Teach Your AI Agents How You Wor
 k
DESCRIPTION:All Things AI (Live)\nThe difference between an AI that gives 
 generic answers and an AI that works like a trusted teammate comes down to
  one thing: **skills.**\nA skill is a reusable playbook — your rules\, y
 our voice\, your process — written down once so your AI can apply it eve
 ry time.\n\nWrite it once\, and every draft comes out in your voice. Every
  report follows your format. Every task runs your way\, without having to 
 re-explain yourself in every chat.\nMark Hinkle\, CEO of Peripety Labs\, p
 ublisher of The AIE Network\, and co-organizer of the All Things AI confer
 ence\, will show you how to write your first skill — and how the same fi
 le can work across the AI tools you already use.\n\n### What You'll Learn\
 n\n• **What a skill is — and why it can be more powerful than prompt e
 ngineering**\n• **The anatomy of a skill file** — simpler than you thi
 nk\; it's just structured text\n• **Skills for yourself vs. skills for y
 our agents** — same idea\, two powerful payoffs\n• **How one skill fil
 e compounds** — write once\, reuse everywhere\n• **The superpower: cha
 ining skills** — link them into a pipeline where one skill's output feed
 s the next\, allowing a single request to run your entire workflow end to 
 end\n\n### Who This Is For\n\nAnyone who uses AI tools regularly and is ti
 red of repeating themselves.\n\n**No technical background required.**\n\n*
 *Free to attend.** The video link will be visible after you RSVP.
