SUMMARY:Lunch and Learn: Vibe Coding\, Take Two — Drop the Vibes\, Ship 
 Production Apps
DESCRIPTION:All Things AI (Live)\nIn Part One\, you saw how AI can build a
  working web app from a plain-English description. Now for the honest foll
 ow-up: **what does it take to ship something real?**\nAn app customers act
 ually use. An app that handles data you care about. An app that **can't fa
 ll over on a Tuesday.**\n\nGood news: you still don't need to become an en
 gineer.\nYou need a lightweight process — the same discipline profession
 al software teams use\, minus the jargon.\n\n**Mark Hinkle\, CEO of Peripe
 ty Labs\, publisher of The AIE Network**\, **and co-organizer of the All T
 hings AI conference\,** will walk through the software development lifecyc
 le the way a business owner should hear it: **as a practical checklist for
  keeping AI-built apps from becoming AI-built messes.**\n\n### What You'll
  Learn\n\n• **The line between a weekend project and a production app** 
 — and how to know which one you're building\n• **A plain-English tour 
 of the software development lifecycle** — plan\, build\, test\, review\,
  deploy\, maintain\n• **How to have AI check its own work** — testing 
 and review without needing to read the code\n• **Version control in one 
 sentence** — and why it can save you at the worst possible moment\n• *
 *When to call in a professional** — and how to be a great client when yo
 u do\n\n### Who This Is For\n\nAnyone who attended Part One\, or anyone wi
 th an AI-built app they're nervous about.\n**Limited technical skills are 
 fully expected.**\n\nMissed Part One? **Come anyway.** We'll open with a q
 uick two-minute recap.\n\n**Free to attend.** The video link will be visib
 le after you RSVP.
